# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Provides information about a SAML authentication domain.

## Example Usage

```terraform
# Get information about a specific SAML authentication domain
data "wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml" "corporate" {
  domain_name = "saml.company.com"
}

# Reference it when creating an authentication domain mapping
resource "wallix-bastion_authdomain_mapping" "saml_admins" {
  domain_id      = data.wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml.corporate.id
  user_group     = "administrators"
  external_group = "bastion-admin"
}

# Get the IdP-initiated SSO URL for this domain
output "saml_idp_initiated_url" {
  value = data.wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml.corporate.idp_initiated_url
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Lookup Key

- `domain_name`: The SAML authentication domain name to look up (Required). The data source
  fails if no authentication domain with this name exists.

### Returned Attributes

- **id**: Internal Bastion ID, usable as `domain_id` in `wallix-bastion_authdomain_mapping`.
- **auth_domain_name**, **label**, **description**, **default_email_domain**,
  **default_language**, **is_default**: Domain identification and defaults.
- **force_authn**: Whether the service provider forces re-authentication at the identity
  provider on every login instead of reusing an existing IdP session.
- **idp_initiated_url**: The URL used to start an IdP-initiated SSO flow for this domain.
- **external_auths**, **secondary_auth**: Lists of related external/secondary authentication
  domain references.

### Usage in Resources

Use the returned `id` as the `domain_id` when creating a `wallix-bastion_authdomain_mapping`
resource to map SAML groups/roles to Bastion user groups.
